=== set-up: scratch keys, a scratch repository, an effort with an identity
  PASS: both efforts' identities are set through git-identity's real scripts
  PASS: trees one and two are cut and committed through git-worktree and git-commit

=== mount-apply.sh: one tree
  $ sh main/mount-apply.sh --effort <S>/space/efforts/<id>-mount-work --name one
    out: {"event":"<S>/space/efforts/<id>-mount-work/events/000006-mount.made.json","target":"<sha>","start":"<sha>","paths":4,"left_alone":1}
    [exit 0]
  PASS: exit 0: target one's tip, start HEAD, 4 paths, mine.txt left alone
  PASS: mount.made read back: by mount-apply.sh, {repo, names, target, start, paths}, its path printed
  PASS: the checkout holds one's work: changed, new (in new folders) and deleted files
  PASS: the index and refs are untouched
  PASS: the mounted paths show as uncommitted changes, mine.txt still there
  PASS: the record, patch and copies are in the checkout's git folder; the record is version 3

